# Kanban agent cards

When a feature file has frontmatter `labels` including **`agent`** (case-insensitive), follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Agent cards.

## User provides

- `## Description` — instructions for the agent (required)
- `## Feature Area` — one backtick-quoted registry label (default: `` `Agent Workflow` ``)

## Agent provides (pre-implementation card review)

- `## Product Paths` — resolved from **Feature Area** via `docs/feature-areas.yaml` (no `tests/`)
- `## Product Methods` — scripts, symbols, and doc sections the work will touch
- `## Tests` — **Files**, **Methods**, **Verify (agent)**
- `## Docs` — doc paths + § hints
- `## Acceptance Criteria` — behavior-only bullets `[ ]`
- `## Decisions` — concrete plan before `in-progress`

## Phased epics

Closed epic history and in-flight manifests: `docs/epics-closed.yaml`, anchor **`## Epic cards`**,
[docs/governance/audit-and-compaction.md](../../docs/governance/audit-and-compaction.md). **Stale drift
spawns:** close **Superseded** when parity checks pass — handbook § Stale spawns. Signatures:
`governance-compaction-drift-alert`, `governance-duplication-automation`, `governance-epic-completion-audit`.

## Workflow

1. Confirm **Description** and **Feature Area** present (default Feature Area if omitted: `Agent Workflow`)
2. Classify user **prompt verb** before edits — `review` / bare `@path` → ask-only; `implement` / `update` / `spawn` → agent ([kanban-card-gates.mdc](kanban-card-gates.mdc) §2; Signature: `kanban-prompt-ask-vs-agent`)
3. Resolve **Feature Area** → **Product Paths** + **Product Methods** + **Tests** + **Docs**
4. Fill **Acceptance Criteria** and **Decisions** on the card
5. `todo` → `in-progress` → implement per **Decisions**
6. Staged pytests green; update `docs/feature-areas.yaml` and `docs/` when registry or user docs change
7. Mark **Acceptance Criteria** `[x]` → `review` → user QA-complete / Done

## Card Done — lessons learned

When the user signals **QA-complete / Done**, the **agent** moves the agent card to `done/` and
runs Card Done **same turn** (Signature: `card-done-agent-move-qa-complete`). Checklist:
[kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Card Done — lessons learned capture;
gel3/gel4/gel5 archive and epic summary pointers in [reference.md § Spawn, epics, and drift](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#spawn-epics-and-drift).

## Card Done `artifacts:` — registry yaml

When capturing lessons that reference registry YAML under `docs/` (`lessons-index.yaml`, `feature-areas.yaml`), use an explicit extension on `doc:` (e.g. `doc:lessons-index.yaml`). Extensionless registry stems are skipped by the parser (Signature: `artifacts-doc-yaml-normalize`).
See [docs/governance/lessons-and-coverage.md](../../docs/governance/lessons-and-coverage.md) §
Lessons captured `artifacts:` schema (Signature: `docs-governance-split`).

## Code edits on agent cards

Python touched by the card must keep lines ≤ **100** characters (`pyproject.toml` `line-length = 100`; pre-commit ruff E501). Wrap strings and split long markdown-in-Python before commit.

